WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.440 --> 00:00:03.200
The concept of beauty
and who is considered beautiful

00:00:03.280 --> 00:00:06.400
has been a core part of the
human experience for millennia.

00:00:06.480 --> 00:00:09.760
And it has long affected
a wide range of social outcomes,

00:00:10.520 --> 00:00:12.200
from partner choices,

00:00:12.280 --> 00:00:13.760
to hiring decisions,

00:00:13.840 --> 00:00:15.680
to life satisfaction.

00:00:15.760 --> 00:00:18.600
So it’s no wonder we humans
have a long history

00:00:18.680 --> 00:00:20.800
of trying to optimise
our beauty.

00:00:20.880 --> 00:00:24.080
And arguably,
that’s intensifying in modern life.

00:00:28.680 --> 00:00:30.240
We are living today in the most

00:00:30.320 --> 00:00:32.920
prolific visual culture in history.

00:00:33.200 --> 00:00:38.160
The obsession with beauty also stems
from new pressures and new freedoms

00:00:38.240 --> 00:00:41.200
people are experiencing
in global capitalism today.

00:00:41.480 --> 00:00:44.800
Many people have more partner choice
than they did before

00:00:44.880 --> 00:00:48.760
as urbanisation grows
and more people date online.

00:00:48.840 --> 00:00:51.800
This means that people
may be competing with others

00:00:51.880 --> 00:00:53.240
more than before.

00:00:53.320 --> 00:00:55.560
More people are also
working in services

00:00:55.640 --> 00:00:57.960
where appearance
can be a job requirement

00:00:58.040 --> 00:01:00.480
and that can contribute
to body anxiety.

00:01:02.240 --> 00:01:05.480
Given the intense social pressure
to look a certain way,

00:01:05.560 --> 00:01:08.400
there’s no surprise that
the beauty business is booming -

00:01:08.480 --> 00:01:14.120
the industry is currently valued
at around $532 billion.

00:01:14.200 --> 00:01:15.520
In 2019,

00:01:15.600 --> 00:01:20.160
globally there were over 11 million
cosmetic surgical procedures

00:01:20.720 --> 00:01:25.160
and over 13 million non-surgical
procedures, such as Botox.

00:01:25.720 --> 00:01:28.480
Of course, there is no one way
of being beautiful,

00:01:28.560 --> 00:01:31.960
but every year brings an abundance
of treatments and products

00:01:32.040 --> 00:01:34.360
that promise new ways
to try and achieve it.

00:01:34.760 --> 00:01:38.640
Like the notorious vampire facial
of the 2010s,

00:01:38.720 --> 00:01:41.600
also known as the platelet-rich
plasma facial.

00:01:42.080 --> 00:01:46.920
First, a sample of your own blood
is taken and then the plasma -

00:01:47.000 --> 00:01:50.080
the liquid part of your blood
that carries cells and proteins -

00:01:50.160 --> 00:01:54.400
is extracted then injected
back into your face.

00:01:54.840 --> 00:01:57.960
Or, in more recent times,
a range of skin products

00:01:58.040 --> 00:02:00.400
containing snail excretions.

00:02:00.480 --> 00:02:03.040
Though neither of these
treatments have proven results.  

00:02:03.400 --> 00:02:05.440
But before you go running
into the garden

00:02:05.520 --> 00:02:07.320
to interfere with some molluscs,

00:02:07.400 --> 00:02:10.240
you might want to ask yourself
if any of these treatments

00:02:10.320 --> 00:02:13.160
and products actually
make you more beautiful.

00:02:13.600 --> 00:02:16.200
Is it even possible to get
an objective assessment

00:02:16.280 --> 00:02:19.760
as to how beautiful - or not -
you actually are?

00:02:20.680 --> 00:02:24.920
Qoves Studio is an Australian based
company who claim to offer just that.

00:02:25.000 --> 00:02:28.160
Using machine learning,
Qoves takes in-depth measurements

00:02:28.240 --> 00:02:31.480
of your facial features,
and then shows you how you compare

00:02:31.560 --> 00:02:33.760
to others within your own ethnicity.

00:02:33.840 --> 00:02:37.120
A useful service
or downright terrifying? 

00:02:37.600 --> 00:02:40.720
At Qoves we have a comprehensive
report where we measure

00:02:40.800 --> 00:02:43.760
your facial features
against scientific standards

00:02:43.840 --> 00:02:45.920
and then evaluate how far off you are

00:02:46.000 --> 00:02:48.800
from the "perfect face".

00:02:49.200 --> 00:02:50.560
Now, there is no perfect face,

00:02:50.640 --> 00:02:54.160
but generally these standards
of scientific measurement

00:02:54.240 --> 00:02:56.000
are the ones that
plastic surgeons would use,

00:02:56.080 --> 00:02:59.560
and so it provides a background
briefing before you go in for surgery

00:02:59.640 --> 00:03:01.040
if that's what you're interested in.

00:03:01.120 --> 00:03:03.840
But is this pursuit
of perfection healthy?

00:03:03.920 --> 00:03:05.720
Shouldn’t we love the skin
we’re in?

00:03:06.200 --> 00:03:09.640
We're providing you with the research
in a nicely packaged way,

00:03:09.720 --> 00:03:10.880
but we always encourage you

00:03:10.960 --> 00:03:13.000
to critically think
about your own surgery

00:03:13.080 --> 00:03:15.280
and to think about
how beauty actually affects you.

00:03:15.360 --> 00:03:18.640
Is it important? Is it important
enough to warrant surgery? 

00:03:19.120 --> 00:03:23.160
If cosmetic surgery or applying
snail mucus doesn’t appeal to you,

00:03:23.240 --> 00:03:25.520
there are thankfully
some less extreme ways

00:03:25.600 --> 00:03:27.320
of optimising your beauty.

00:03:30.480 --> 00:03:33.640
If you have too much sun exposure,
UV exposure,

00:03:33.720 --> 00:03:35.800
this can cause damage to your skin

00:03:35.880 --> 00:03:37.280
and the cells in the skin.

00:03:37.360 --> 00:03:39.880
The DNA may undergo mutations,

00:03:39.960 --> 00:03:42.240
which may eventually
lead to skin cancer.

00:03:42.600 --> 00:03:46.960
Because the UV rays can penetrate
deeper into the skin,

00:03:47.040 --> 00:03:50.640
they also damage the collagen
and the elastic fibres

00:03:50.720 --> 00:03:53.920
that are in the lower layer
of the skin. 

00:03:54.000 --> 00:03:56.520
And this is what causes
the deep wrinkles.

00:03:56.600 --> 00:03:58.080
So when you're out in the sun

00:03:58.160 --> 00:04:00.280
for a long time then you should wear

00:04:00.360 --> 00:04:02.160
a broad spectrum suncream

00:04:02.240 --> 00:04:07.720
or clothes that cover your skin
to prevent that skin damage.

00:04:09.960 --> 00:04:14.560
Lack of sleep can release the stress
hormones which are bad for our skin,

00:04:14.640 --> 00:04:18.120
also, the skin has its own
internal clock

00:04:18.200 --> 00:04:20.280
and so skin cells are programmed

00:04:20.360 --> 00:04:22.280
to grow and repair

00:04:22.360 --> 00:04:23.840
at night while we sleep. 

00:04:23.920 --> 00:04:25.880
A good night's sleep
can be subjective,

00:04:25.960 --> 00:04:29.520
but on average it’s anywhere
between six and nine hours.

00:04:30.760 --> 00:04:34.040
Genetic epidemiologist Tim Spector
says the role of diet

00:04:34.120 --> 00:04:36.760
in conditions such as acne
is still unclear.

00:04:36.840 --> 00:04:39.240
But he believes that keeping
the microbes in your gut

00:04:39.320 --> 00:04:42.360
in good working order,
through reducing processed food

00:04:42.440 --> 00:04:45.000
and eating a wide range
of fruit and vegetables,

00:04:45.080 --> 00:04:47.440
should help your skin’s
health generally.

00:04:47.840 --> 00:04:50.600
So in the future,
we will be able to tell you

00:04:50.680 --> 00:04:53.280
which foods you should be eating

00:04:53.360 --> 00:04:55.800
to enhance this particular type

00:04:55.880 --> 00:04:58.200
of microbe that could help
your skin health.

00:04:58.280 --> 00:05:01.560
At the moment,
we're just giving general advice

00:05:01.640 --> 00:05:07.520
to increase the helpful microbes in
your gut and reduce the harmful ones.

00:05:07.600 --> 00:05:10.680
You might think all this beautifying
is deeply superficial -

00:05:11.280 --> 00:05:13.080
but perhaps this pursuit of beauty

00:05:13.160 --> 00:05:15.520
is part of what makes
our species unique. 

00:05:16.040 --> 00:05:20.440
The Kadiwéu people in Brazil
elaborately paint their faces,

00:05:20.520 --> 00:05:24.000
the Nuba in the Sudan practice
scarification,

00:05:24.080 --> 00:05:29.080
the tattoo, a Polynesian word,
is widespread across the Pacific.

00:05:29.160 --> 00:05:32.320
Beauty can have an irresistible pull
for humans,

00:05:32.400 --> 00:05:35.040
but we are fundamentally different
from other animals

00:05:35.120 --> 00:05:38.520
in that we do not accept
our bodies as they are. 

